SSEECCUURRIITTYY CCOONNSSIIDDEERRAATTIIOONNSS
     Note that in some configurations, bbhhyyvveellooaadd will execute guest loader
     scripts in the context of the host machine.  Note, however, that
     bbhhyyvveellooaadd will enter a capsicum(4) sandbox before it loads the _o_s_-_l_o_a_d_e_r
     or executes any loader scripts.  On the host filesystem, the sandbox will
     only have access to the path specified by the --hh flag, the contents of
     the _/_b_o_o_t directory if --ll was not specified, and the chosen console de‐
     vice.

     Note that the guest loader scripts are already subject to some limita‐
     tions that are not relaxed simply because we are running in userland.
     For instance, any I/O on the loader's “host” device that can be done in
     loader scripts is limited to the interface that bbhhyyvveellooaadd provides, which
     itself will restrict paths that can be touched to those within a speci‐
     fied --hh directory, if any.  Access to files within _/_b_o_o_t inside the sand‐
     box would require arbitrary code execution in userboot, and userboot is
     usually provided by the host machine rather than anything that is a part
     of the guest image.  All access to the --hh directory as well as _/_b_o_o_t is
     strictly read-only in the sandbox.

